;
; expect: instance-key redeclaration divergence (IDENTICAL-OR-ABSENT, full
; context). Three redecls of `rel`: @key(A), then an UNKEYED redecl, then
; @key(B). The unkeyed middle decl carries no key and inherits silently. The
; divergence is @key(B) vs the canonical @key(A), but they are NOT adjacent:
; the unkeyed redecl sits between them. The old immediate-previous-only check
; short-circuited on the unkeyed middle decl (empty key), so @key(B) vs @key(A)
; was NEVER compared and `InstanceKeys()` silently returned the first key {A}.
; Compiles rc=0 under the immediate-previous check (a LOST CHECK); rejects rc=1
; once the check resolves the canonical contract across the WHOLE context.
; Distinct query name `q` so no cross-kind AddDecl collision masks the check.
#message edge_2(u64 A, u64 B).
#local rel(u64 A, u64 B) @key(A).
#local rel(u64 A, u64 B).
#local rel(u64 A, u64 B) @key(B).
rel(A, B) : edge_2(A, B).
#query q(bound u64 A, free u64 B).
q(A, B) : rel(A, B).
